# Executive Summary XML Reference Patterns

This reference contains exact XML patterns extracted from the template for precise replication.

## Document Namespaces

```xml
xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main"
xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships"
xmlns:wp="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/wordprocessingDrawing"
xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main"
xmlns:pic="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/picture"
```

## docx-js to XML Mapping

When using docx-js, these are the key property mappings:

| docx-js Property | XML Equivalent | Notes |
|-----------------|----------------|-------|
| `width: { size: X, type: WidthType.DXA }` | `<w:tcW w:w="X" w:type="dxa"/>` | Cell width in twentieths of a point |
| `width: { size: 100, type: WidthType.PERCENTAGE }` | `<w:tblW w:w="5000" w:type="pct"/>` | Table width as percentage |
| `columnWidths: [X, Y, Z]` | `<w:tblGrid><w:gridCol w:w="X"/><w:gridCol w:w="Y"/>...` | **CRITICAL** for proper column sizing |
| `shading: { fill: "COLOR", type: ShadingType.CLEAR, color: "auto" }` | `<w:shd w:val="clear" w:color="auto" w:fill="COLOR"/>` | Must include all three properties |
| `borders: { top: {...}, ... }` | `<w:tblBorders>...</w:tblBorders>` | Table-level borders |
| `verticalAlign: VerticalAlign.CENTER` | `<w:vAlign w:val="center"/>` | Cell vertical alignment |

## Common Table Rendering Issues

| Issue | Cause | Solution |
|-------|-------|----------|
| Columns collapse | Missing `columnWidths` array | Always specify columnWidths in Table constructor |
| Uneven columns | Widths don't match content | Calculate based on content type guidelines |
| Missing shading | Incomplete shading object | Include fill, type: ShadingType.CLEAR, and color: "auto" |
| Broken highlight column | Last cell empty/unstyled | Use placeholder "â€”" with highlight styling |
| Text overflow | Column too narrow | Increase DXA width, abbreviate text if needed |
| Borders not showing | Wrong border definition | Use insideHorizontal/insideVertical for inner borders |

